  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25890180",
      "title": "Understanding Type Inference",
      "sourceHash": "a2c9e753d9788ac14d19b641718b8a9df2fa8f2b263226a4d13d8ba956f080d3",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.05,
          "end": 4.8,
          "en": "Now, that we have learned about those base types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.8,
          "end": 8.45,
          "en": "before I dive into functions and parameters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.45,
          "end": 11.5,
          "en": "I wanna talk about type inference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.5,
          "end": 14.36,
          "en": "In all those examples, which are listed here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.36,
          "end": 18.45,
          "en": "I always declared a variable with a type assigned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.45,
          "end": 22.6,
          "en": "And then in a second step, I set a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.6,
          "end": 26.32,
          "en": "Now, often in programming, you do that in one step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.32,
          "end": 28.5,
          "en": "You create a variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.5,
          "end": 31.983,
          "en": "and you then already immediately assign an initial value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.95,
          "end": 36.48,
          "en": "So therefore here let's talk about type inference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.48,
          "end": 38.96,
          "en": "And let me show you what that is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.96,
          "end": 41.35,
          "en": "Let's say we have another variable down here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.35,
          "end": 45.26,
          "en": "The course variable. And in that course variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.26,
          "end": 47.49,
          "en": "I wanna store the name of a course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.49,
          "end": 50.84,
          "en": "like react the complete guide.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.84,
          "end": 52.33,
          "en": "Like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.33,
          "end": 55.85,
          "en": "Now, if I create this variable like this, and thereafter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.85,
          "end": 59.972,
          "en": "I try to store a number for an example, the course ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.972,
          "end": 63.13,
          "en": "then you will see that I get an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.13,
          "end": 66.57300000000001,
          "en": "because the type number is not assignable to type string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.5,
          "end": 70.4,
          "en": "But why am I getting this error?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.4,
          "end": 73.97,
          "en": "After all, I don't define a type anywhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 73.97,
          "end": 77.91,
          "en": "Well, here TypeScript used its powerful feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.91,
          "end": 80.2,
          "en": "of type inference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.2,
          "end": 84.03999999999999,
          "en": "By default, TypeScript tries to infer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.03999999999999,
          "end": 86.23,
          "en": "as many types as possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.23,
          "end": 89.77,
          "en": "So it tries to know which types are used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.77,
          "end": 94.11,
          "en": "where, without you explicitly stating those types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.11,
          "end": 96.763,
          "en": "Which means that you need to write less code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 97.62,
          "end": 102.03,
          "en": "I could also set my type here as we learned it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.03,
          "end": 105.57,
          "en": "That would not be wrong, but it's redundant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 105.57,
          "end": 109.07,
          "en": "because if you immediately initialize this variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 109.07,
          "end": 113.4,
          "en": "with a type TypeScript, will look at the value type here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 113.4,
          "end": 117.32,
          "en": "So it will see that we stored a string in that variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 117.32,
          "end": 120.19,
          "en": "And it will then use that value type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 120.19,
          "end": 123.97,
          "en": "as an inferred type for this variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 123.97,
          "end": 128.34,
          "en": "And if you then try to assign a different type thereafter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 128.34,
          "end": 132.51,
          "en": "you'll get an error, because of type inference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 132.51,
          "end": 134.81,
          "en": "And it is considered a good practice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 134.81,
          "end": 139.31,
          "en": "and a good idea to embrace that type inference feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 139.31,
          "end": 143.25,
          "en": "So to not unnecessarily specify the type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 143.25,
          "end": 146.71,
          "en": "in addition, you can do that you can explicitly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 146.71,
          "end": 149.57,
          "en": "state to type, but it's really redundant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 149.57,
          "end": 152.66,
          "en": "It just means more word from your side and therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 152.66,
          "end": 154.18,
          "en": "you should not do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 154.18,
          "end": 155.82999999999998,
          "en": "You should instead stick",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 155.82999999999998,
          "end": 160.24,
          "en": "to that type inference and use it whenever possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 160.24,
          "end": 163.36,
          "en": "And that's another super important feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 163.36,
          "end": 165.313,
          "en": "which I wanted to highlight here.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
